	(text "Polarity: CM5 TX_P -> PETp0 (49), TX_N -> PETn0 (47), PERp0 (43) -> RX_P, PERn0 (41) -> RX_N. The CM5IO reference wires both pairs inverted (TX_P to 47, RX_P to 41), which PCIe link training tolerates; either works."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 276 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1c7346be-de73-5e5b-87d6-dfb1a0be0922")
	)
	(text "Only PCIe lane 0 is wired (x1). PET = host transmit (CM5 TX, AC caps on the module). PER = host receive: per the M.2 spec the SSD carries its own TX caps, so R502/R503 are 0R; the same 0402 pads take 100n if a module without caps turns up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 280.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7843531c-4e0b-5b50-b11d-a25f847e8876")
	)
	(text "PEDET (pin 69) is pulled up and read by GPIO19: an M.2 SATA module grounds it, and the software refuses the bay instead of trying PCIe."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 285 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8b38772b-7ec0-5eb0-a14c-5f2c967fcdc2")
	)
	(text "Door switch SW3 to GPIO4 (software pull-up): closed = low = door shut. Software powers the slot (M2_PWR_EN, GPIO27 -> U50) and rescans PCIe."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 289.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2825cb89-9175-5bed-bbc0-08699d5dc2bd")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
